    <string name="tepco_login_title">Log in to TEPCO</string>
    <string name="elec_not_connected_detail">After you log in to くらしTEPCO web, the bills of the last 25 months and the usage of the current period so far are loaded and saved on this device.</string>
    <string name="elec_no_data">No electricity data yet</string>
    <string name="elec_chart_note">A “month” in the chart is TEPCO\'s billing month, not a calendar month: TEPCO reads the meter once a month, so “October” is the usage from the September reading day to the day before the October reading day, usually mid-September to mid-October. Usage and amounts are the bill records on くらしTEPCO web (billed amount, incl. tax). Every login loads the last 25 months and replaces the data saved on this device as a whole. The current period is not in the chart; while last month\'s bill is not out yet, the card above shows the actual usage and amount of the current period so far (not a forecast). Swipe left or right to see other years, long-press the chart to preview values, and tap a point to see its details.</string>
    <string name="elec_bill_confirmed">Confirmed bill</string>
    <string name="elec_bill_provisional">Bill not confirmed yet (provisional amount)</string>
    <string name="refresh_advice_title">About refreshing</string>
    <string name="refresh_advice_detail">This is the time the data was last loaded. Bills only change once a month, so refreshing once a month, or only when you need it, is enough; there is no need to refresh every day: TEPCO needs a new login for every refresh, and frequent visits to the official services serve no purpose.</string>
    <string name="elec_error_login_required">Log in to TEPCO again</string>
    <string name="elec_error_login_required_detail">The TEPCO data was not updated: the last login has expired (after about 30 minutes). Log in again with “Log in and update” on this page; the latest data is loaded after the login. The data saved on this device is not affected.</string>
    <string name="elec_error_login_failed">The login did not finish (%s). Please log in again.</string>
